    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.74,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.07,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.73 from 7 h onward. I diluted retained aliquots to check whether the reader was saturating. At 18 h, a 3x dilution read 0.2435, which is 0.730 after correcting for dilution. Two 10x replicates read 0.0763 and 0.0770, which is about 0.766 after correcting. At 12 h, a 20x dilution read 0.0353, which is 0.706 after correcting. The undiluted 18 h reading was 0.728. All dilution-corrected values are within about 5% of the undiluted reading and show no systematic rise with dilution. If the reader were saturating, the corrected values would be well above the undiluted reading. The plateau therefore looks like real stationary phase."
  },
